    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0262" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg186"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.60i31/27</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Estonia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 654</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1935-03-22"
                            >March 22, 1935</date>.<lb/>[Received April 4.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith copies
                    of a Memorandum handed to me at Tallinn, on February 27, by Mr. Wirgo, Director
                    of the Foreign Trade Bureau of the Estonian Foreign Office, with reference to
                    the desire of the Estonian Government to modify the American-Estonian Treaty of
                    Friendship, Commerce and Consular Rights, of December 23, 1925. The substance of
                    this Memorandum was communicated to the Department in my telegram (No. 3) from
                    Tallinn, February 27, 5 p.m.;<anchor n="17" xml:id="d149-f1"/> and it is to this
                    Memorandum that references were made in the Department’s telegram of March 21, 5
                    p.m., to the Tallinn Legation,<anchor n="17" xml:id="d149-f2"/> and in my reply
                    (No. 29, March 22, 2 p.m.) of today’s date.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d149-f3"/></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. V. A. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d149-a1.xml" xpointer="d149-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
